# loom workspace state (created by `loom init`)
# Every .loom directory holds local state - shared state under .loom/work (a
# real directory in the main repo, a symlink in worktrees), the per-worktree
# spool files, and the derived context cache - and is never committed. The
# pattern has no slash, so it matches at any depth: loom run from a
# subdirectory creates a .loom there. A workspace created before this
# migration keeps the legacy .work forever (see doc/plans, "Back-compat").
# CRITICAL: both the directory and symlink forms of .work are needed - git
# ignores a symlink by its own name, not by resolving where it points.
.work/
.work
.loom

# Rust build artifacts
target/
!loom/src/commands/target/

# loom plan artifacts (completed and review copies)
doc/plans/DONE-*
doc/plans/REVIEW-*
doc/plans/**/DONE-*
doc/plans/**/REVIEW-*

# loom worktrees (isolated stage execution)
# CRITICAL: Both patterns needed - directory form and symlink form
.worktrees/
.worktrees
web/node_modules/
ISSUES.md

data/*
doc/plans/completed/DONE-PLAN-codex-implementer-subagents.md
doc/plans/completed/DONE-PLAN-simplify-cli.md

